# Build context for cic/Dockerfile, which builds from ./cic and only ./cic.
#
# Docker reads this file from the CONTEXT ROOT, so it is this file - not
# the one at the repo root - that governs the image. The repo-root
# .dockerignore existed solely to allowlist cic-poc/frontend into a
# repo-root context; the frontend came out of the image on 2026-08-17 and
# that file went with it.
#
# An exclusion list rather than an allowlist, because the context is now
# one tree whose contents are known. cic/ is 170MB and 154MB of that is
# texts/, so these four lines are most of the difference between a 16MB
# context and a 170MB one.

# Primary-source texts. Nothing under runtime/app/ reads them - the
# serving path reads deploy/ (generated views), records/ and engine/.
texts/
# CI-only gates (isolation, transcript window). They run in GitHub
# Actions against the repo, never inside the served container.
checks/
# Generated at build time by runtime/scripts/build_indices.py. A
# host-built copy must never be admitted - the image has to contain
# indices built against the records in THIS image, or the assertion step
# is checking someone else's work.
runtime/vector_store/
# Ephemeral session logs. Never seed a container with someone else's.
runtime/transcripts/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
